# DuetSoftwareFramework packages from a separately published build of our
# own, installed in place of the Duet3D archive's.
#
# One line per package:
#
#   <package> sha256:<checksum of the published .deb> <https location>
#
# The DSF packages pin each other to one exact version and check it again at
# runtime, so a build of our own is installed as a whole: every package that
# pkg/build.sh --packages=progs,dwc,meta produces in the fork, at a version
# <dsf.version>+<suffix> (3.7.0~rc.2+mp.1 for a modified 3.7.0~rc.2).
# duetwebcontrol is among them: the build packages our fork of Duet Web
# Control, Meltingplot/DuetWebControl, at a version of the same form, and the
# meta package pins it. duetsd and reprapfirmware come from the archive, where
# the build's meta package pins them; reprapfirmware at dsf.rrf_version, which
# the meta package has to accept. An empty list installs the archive's
# packages. Only a published build is taken, checked against the pin: no local
# path, no fallback, a mismatch stops the build. See "Installing a
# DuetSoftwareFramework build of our own" in the README.
#
# A board firmware file is not a package of the build; it goes through
# firmware.list.

# 3.7.0-rc.2+mp.7: upstream v3.7-dev at 3.7.0-rc.2, which moves the
# accelerometers from boards[] to sensors.accelerometers (as the RepRapFirmware
# build in firmware.list reports them) and, since mp.7, brings the object model
# additions, the query flag fix and the file info parser changes of upstream,
# plus our fix for a DCS crash on a non-finite expression result, and Duet Web
# Control from our fork, 3.7.0-rc.2+mp.6, the tag pkg/dwc-version in the fork
# pins, with the CHX 350 operator interface, which leaves machine actions such
# as preheating, homing and filament change to the flow macros of the printer
# configuration, reports a flow as completed only when it reaches its
# `echo ";; Completed"` line, moves the axes while a job is paused and shows
# history and analysis from the QualityAssurance plugin. The release of that
# Duet Web Control also carries the interface's SBC backend, which plugins.list
# pins at the same version. The meta package accepts the firmware of 3.7.0-rc.1
# (pkg/firmware-version in the fork), which dsf.rrf_version installs. Earlier
# builds: mp.6 carried Duet Web Control 3.7.0-rc.2+mp.5, mp.5 3.7.0-rc.2+mp.4,
# mp.4 3.7.0-rc.2+mp.3, mp.3 3.7.0-rc.2+mp.2, mp.9 of 3.7.0-rc.1 brought remote
# sensors on CAN expansion boards, mp.8 checked N line numbers in job and macro
# files, mp.7 RRF-style checksums on numbered lines, mp.6 kept the object model
# in step after an SPI transfer timeout.
